      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-r/q9-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(c) From part (a), the rational expression is 1 + 16x2/(3x −2). [B1] [A1] Multiplying the series in part (b) by 16x2 gives 1 −8x2 −12x3 −18x4 −27x5. Alternatively, multiplying the original numerator by the series through x3 gives these three rows: = 1 + 3 2x + 9 4x2 + 27 8 x3 + . . . −3 2x −9 4x2 −27 8 x3 + . . . , −8x2 −12x3 + . . . = 1 −8x2 −12x3 + . . . The partial-fraction method supplies the fourth and fifth powers too, with the stated expansion with remainder O(x6) . [B1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
