      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-r/q10-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) Use sin(a + b) = sin a cos b + cos a sin b with a = 2θ, b = θ. Expand sin(2θ + θ) = 2 sin θ cos2 θ + (1 −2 sin2 θ) sin θ. [M1] [A1] Using cos2 θ = 1 −sin2 θ [A1] gives 2 sin θ(1 −sin2 θ) + sin θ −2 sin3 θ, hence 3 sin θ −4 sin3 θ . [A1] (b) Differentiate to obtain 3 cos 3θ = 3 cos θ −12 sin2 θ cos θ. [M1] [A1] Divide by 3 and substitute sin2 θ = 1 −cos2 θ: cos 3θ = cos θ −4 cos θ sin2 θ\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
